WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:01.267
Finance ministers

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.335
from around the world

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.570
descended on Washington

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.504
this week as they do

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:05.205
every spring

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:06.973
for annual meetings of the World Bank

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:08.375
and the IMF.

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:09.809
They gathered a worrying time

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:10.710
for the world economy.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.911
The IMF said this week

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.713
that it expects global growth

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.448
to be slower than last year.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:17.484
Only 2.8%.

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:18.551
One of the pressures

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:19.486
weighing the world down.

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:21.788
Of course, is Russia's war with Ukraine.

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:24.157
More now of my exclusive interview

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.226
with Treasury Secretary Janet Yellen.

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:28.595
You must have these IMF meetings.

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:31.297
We're talking about the Russia sanctions.

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:33.500
And I wanted to ask you.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.968
When you look at them,

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:37.404
what is the piece of evidence

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:39.739
you could point to that

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.908
conclusively demonstrates

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.610
that they are actually working

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:46.413
and that Russia is being substantially

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:48.114
deprived of revenues,

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:50.717
that Putin is paying an economic price.

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:53.686
So we've had two objectives from

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:54.687
the outset.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:57.590
One is to deprive Russia of revenue.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:58.892
As you noted,

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:02.495
And the second is to deny him

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:05.932
access to the equipment that he needs

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.002
to provision his

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.670
military adequately

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.972
to conduct this brutal war.

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:16.242
On the revenue side

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:19.379
of our price, caps

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:22.148
that we've put in place on Russian oil

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.884
have lowered

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:27.687
the revenues that Putin is receiving

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:31.991
by roughly 40% over the last year.

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:35.929
He expected to have budget surpluses.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:39.666
He now has very large budget deficits

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.335
in terms of equipment.

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:45.138
We know that we have had great success

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:47.140
in depriving him of the equipment

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.976
that he needs to conduct this war.

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:53.446
This is due to our export controls.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:54.647
And importantly,

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.382
it's not just the United States

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:57.784
acting alone.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.786
It's that we have strong

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:01.788
coalition partners

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:03.690
who are working together

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.725
to put in place sanctions,

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.894
export controls,

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:11.064
and working jointly on enforcement.

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:14.534
He lost over 9000

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:17.036
pieces of heavy equipment

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.605
on the battlefield field,

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:20.640
and we see the Russian,

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.010
the Russians struggling to replace this.

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:26.779
So we see on the battlefield

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:29.682
Russia is now

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:33.553
forced to resort to Iran and North Korea

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:38.091
to try to supply his military.

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:41.461
And we continue to take steps to

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:43.029
make sure

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:45.498
that vision of our sanctions

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:46.766
isn't possible.

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:50.803
But we think his military is really

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:53.973
short of the equipment that they need

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.109
to wage war.

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:57.810
Let me ask you about one of the costs,

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.846
one of the prices of these sanctions,

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:01.681
the way that the United States

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:02.782
has used sanctions.

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.717
Often in this case,

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:07.187
the case of the Iran nuclear deal

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:08.388
is to use

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:09.422
the power of the dollar

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:11.558
as the reserve currency of the world.

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:13.092
But that

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.761
weaponization of the dollar

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:16.829
has produced a reaction

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:19.566
This week, President Lula in Brazil

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:20.166
said,

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:22.202
Why are we all being forced

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:23.403
to use the dollar?

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:24.637
Emmanuel Macron

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:26.539
made reference to the dollar

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:27.273
In that same way

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:29.309
the European Commission has talked about

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:29.909
after Trump

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:31.544
pulled out of the Iran sanctions,

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:32.579
talked about

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:34.080
creating an alternative

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:34.714
to Swift

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:37.483
to the American dominated payment system.

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:38.851
Is there

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:41.454
a danger that we will look back at all

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:42.322
these

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:43.423
these measures and said

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:44.924
this was the moment

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:47.794
that the dollar's hegemony and its status

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:49.996
as a reserve currency began to falter?

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:54.300
So serious risk when we use

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.802
financial sanctions

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:56.436
that are linked

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:58.504
to the role of dollar of the dollar,

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:01.941
that over time it could undermine

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:04.811
the hegemony of the dollar, as you said.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:09.616
But this is an extremely important tool

00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:13.253
we try to use judiciously

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:15.888
and in circumstances

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:17.790
especially when we have

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.359
the support of our allies.

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:21.394
It's not just the United States.

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:24.697
It's a coalition of partners

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:27.433
acting together

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:29.502
to impose these sanctions.

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:33.940
So it is a very effective tool.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:34.741
Of course,

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:38.044
it does create a desire on the part

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:41.681
of China, of Russia, of Iran

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:46.152
to find an alternative but

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:51.524
the dollar is used as a global currency

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:54.961
for reasons that are not easy

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:59.699
for other countries to find

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:01.567
find an alternative

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:04.437
with the same properties.

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:07.173
The US Treasury market is the deepest

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:10.143
and most liquid and safest asset

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:13.513
dollars are widely used.

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:17.550
It's we have very deep

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.218
capital markets

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:20.987
and rule of law

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:23.923
that are essential in a currency

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:25.325
that is going to be used

00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:27.794
globally for transactions.

00:05:28.061 --> 00:05:31.097
And we haven't seen any other country

00:05:32.332 --> 00:05:36.035
that has the

00:05:36.035 --> 00:05:38.071
best basic infrastructure

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:41.107
and institutional infrastructure

00:05:42.075 --> 00:05:44.711
that would enable its currency to serve

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:46.112
a world like this.

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:47.146
We ask you one question

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:48.014
about Ukraine,

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:51.117
about rebuilding Ukraine, resupplying it.

00:05:51.117 --> 00:05:52.885
It's going to take a lot of money.

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:54.654
There are some who say

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:56.923
this money should be taken from Russia's

00:05:56.923 --> 00:05:58.624
frozen central bank reserves.

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:00.093
Would you agree with that?

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:02.895
I think Russia should pay for the damage

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:05.264
that it is done to Ukraine.

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:09.302
So that's a responsibility that I think

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:13.272
the global community expects.

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:15.408
Russia to bear.

00:06:15.408 --> 00:06:16.275
This is something

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:18.511
we're discussing with our partners.

00:06:18.945 --> 00:06:19.779
But

00:06:22.482 --> 00:06:25.218
you know, several legal constraints

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:28.221
on what we can do

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:30.323
with frozen Russian assets

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:33.326
and we're discussing

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:34.193
with our partners

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:36.829
what might lie in the future.

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:39.332
But I think that's the right thing for

00:06:39.332 --> 00:06:41.768
to happen, that Russia should pay

00:06:41.768 --> 00:06:43.669
for the damages that it's caused.

